// A String return stays refused after the pointer wall opened in v0.0.196, and that is the same
// rule rather than an omission: a String is a Burxt value with an OWNER, so accepting one here
// would be a claim about whose memory it is that C has no way to make.
//
// `-> CPointer` plus `c_string_at(p)` says the same thing and says who copied. See
// tests/pass/c_pointer_wall.bx.
external function getenv_like() -> String;
print(getenv_like());
